
I wrote the full project and ran the tests locally. Push 1 passes 7 tests and Push 2 passes 11. All three YAML files parse. I could not build the Docker image here because Docker Desktop isn't running on this machine, and the GitHub Actions pipeline has not run yet. The first real check of the build and deploy jobs will be your Push 1.

The app is a Flask web page with a menu. A command-line `input()` menu would crash inside a Kubernetes pod because the pod has no keyboard input, so it has to be a web page.

How the five stages map:
1. **Source code:** the files below, written in VS Code.
2. **Version control:** Git, pushed to GitHub.
3. **Continuous integration:** a GitHub Actions job that checks out the code, installs dependencies and runs pytest.
4. **Build:** a Docker image tagged `v<run number>-<short commit id>` and pushed to Docker Hub.
5. **Deployment:** a Kubernetes cluster (kind) created inside the GitHub runner. The Deployment uses that push's exact tag, and a NodePort Service exposes the app.

